      "writtenOn": "2026-06-23T15:38:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I suppose it\u0027s just 10-bit and 12-bit. How common is this and would it be better to lift it to 16 bit unorm so we don\u0027t lose precision? It shouldn\u0027t take too much work to add a kGray16 format, although gray is an awkward colortype since it\u0027s not renderable.  \n\nSkia\u0027s SkYUVInfo is also likely going to add support for 10-bit and 12-bit values stored in 16 bits. Can the codecs produce YUV 400 as SkYUV metadata instead of having to go to a flattened SkImageInfo?",
      "parentUuid": "e3048b7e_db35b5d9",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 252,
        "startChar": 25,
        "endLine": 252,
        "endChar": 54
      },
      "revId": "3d26e1ee38dc592042602ae90a278816bb79a1aa",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
